WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
It started out that you plowed behind a mule.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.560
You had a plow—you followed a mule or two,

3
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:14.400
whichever the case may be . . . you did all the work which was manual at the time.

4
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:19.500
Even my sugarcane which I remember just briefly, it was all manual.

5
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:27.980
You cut it manually, you loaded it onto a cart, the mules drove the cart to the,

6
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:36.960
what we call the derrick which was a lift that put the chain that held the cane into a truck,

7
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.840
it went to the sugar mill and was processed there.

8
00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.640
So it was all manual.

9
00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:51.420
During the war, World War II, there was a lot of changes that came about during the war and immediately following the war.

10
00:00:51.420 --> 00:01:00.100
For instance, we were still cutting cane by hand during World War II and only toward the end of the war that we mechanized.

11
00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:08.672
And we had mechanical harvesters that went in and cut the cane and laid it on the road and then you had to grab it,

12
00:01:08.672 --> 00:01:15.040
pick it up and put it in the carts, tractors, and it went onto the mill that way.

13
00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.000
The hand didn’t touch it then.

14
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:31.100
Now you have, just using that example, you have what they call combine harvesters which chops the cane now and blows it into a cart;

15
00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:37.060
goes to the mill and comes right into the conveyor belts into the mill.

16
00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:46.740
I mean, the educational background of the farmers just increased dramatically, particularly at the college level.

17
00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:59.820
First step, then later on even at the master’s level and then very few, but some, at the PhD level that are actually managing farms.

18
00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:05.980
Then that brought in . . . the technical development brought in a lot of consultant type work.

19
00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:14.640
And most of them that I know have PhDs in either soil science or entomology or some technical work.

20
00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:19.720
And the farmers have increased their capabilities.

21
00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:25.720
What about other things, like mechanical technological changes or even telephones?

22
00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.880
Did those things change throughout the years?

23
00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.400
Oh, completely.

24
00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:32.420
Anything notable that stands out in your mind?

25
00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.680
Well, number one, telephones.

26
00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:40.600
I couldn’t pick up my phone here and make a call when I first came to Baton Rouge into the state office.

27
00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:49.860
I had to get a signed receipt from my supervisor that it was all right for me to call a county agent in X Parish.
